  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Database, tables and keys"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A *database* is an organised collection of related data; a database management system (DBMS) is software that creates, stores, updates and retrieves that data while keeping it consistent and secure. Data is kept in tables. Each row is a record (one voucher or one account) and each column is a field (date, voucher number, account code, amount). A primary key is a field whose value is unique for every record, such as a voucher number or account code. A foreign key links one table to another, for example the account code in a Vouchers table refers to the Accounts table."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Table = rows (records) × columns (fields)"
    },
    {
     "en": "Primary key: unique for each record"
    },
    {
     "en": "Foreign key: links related *tables*"
    },
    {
     "en": "Each field has a data type: text, number, date"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A database is an organised collection of related data; a database management system (DBMS) is software that creates, stores, updates and retrieves that data while keeping it consistent and secure. Data is kept in tables. Each row is a record (one voucher or one account) and each column is a field (date, voucher number, account code, amount). A primary key is a field whose value is unique for every record, such as a voucher number or account code. A foreign key links one table to another, for example the account code in a Vouchers table refers to the Accounts table."
   },
   "reveal": true,
   "voice": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A database is an organised collection of related data; a database management system DBMS is software that creates, stores, updates and retrieves that data while keeping it consistent and secure. Data is kept in tables. Each row is a record (one voucher or one account) and each column is a field (date, voucher number, account code, amount). A primary key is a field whose value is unique for every record, such as a voucher number or account code. A foreign key links one table to another, for example the account code in a Vouchers table refers to the Accounts table. Table equals rows records times columns fields."
     }
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Primary key: unique for each record."
     }
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Foreign key: links related tables."
     }
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Each field has a data type: text, number, date."
     }
    }
   ]
  },
